# WAAMTO ERP Rules v3.0

> ERP-specific development rules.

---

# Purpose

Maintain a modular, scalable and production-ready ERP while preserving the approved architecture.

---

# Architecture

Always follow the approved ERP architecture.

Never move business logic into the platform/core unless explicitly designed for shared platform functionality.

---

# Module Development

Every feature must belong to the correct module.

Avoid duplicate functionality across modules.

Prefer extending existing modules over creating new ones.

---

# Business Logic

Keep business rules inside the owning module.

Reuse shared services where appropriate.

---

# Database

Maintain data integrity.

Reuse existing tables and relationships when suitable.

Avoid unnecessary schema changes.

---

# APIs

Maintain backward compatibility unless a breaking change is approved.

Reuse existing endpoints when practical.

---

# UI

Follow the existing design system.

Reuse layouts, tables, forms, dialogs and shared components.

Do not redesign screens unless requested.

---

# Performance

Consider the impact on:

- database queries
- API performance
- page load
- large datasets

Optimise when justified.

---

# Security

Respect:

- authentication
- RBAC
- tenant isolation
- input validation

Never bypass security controls.

---

# Multi-Tenancy

Ensure tenant isolation is preserved.

Do not expose cross-tenant data.

Verify company, branch and warehouse scope where applicable.

---

# Integrations

Preserve compatibility with approved ERP integrations.

Do not break existing workflows.

---

# Testing

Validate:

- business workflow
- affected APIs
- UI behaviour
- permissions
- data integrity
- likely regression areas

Test everything reasonably affected by the change.

---

# Documentation

Update documentation only when user-facing behaviour, APIs or configuration changes.

